Boarding Management System – Functional & Technical Requirements Specification
Document Type: Functional & Technical Requirements
Module: Boarding Management
System: School Management System
Primary Operational Authority: Director of Discipline (DOD)
Version: 1.0
Status: Development / Redesign Specification
________________________________________
1. Purpose
The Boarding Management Module is responsible for managing the complete operational lifecycle of boarding students, including:
•	Dormitory management
•	Patron / Matron management
•	Student assignment
•	Student leave requests and approvals
•	Parent leave requests
•	Gate exit and entry control
•	Boarding biometric attendance
•	Dining management
•	Dining attendance
•	Boarding schedules and time windows
•	Student status tracking
•	Parent notifications and SMS alerts
•	Security verification
•	Operational reporting
•	Escalation and exception management
•	Complete audit trail
The system must treat the Director of Discipline (DOD) as the central operational authority for boarding operations.
The DOD reports administratively to the Head Teacher / Principal, but operationally, boarding activities are controlled through the DOD.
________________________________________
2. Boarding Operational Hierarchy
The recommended operational hierarchy is:
Head Teacher / Principal / School Admin
↓
Director of Discipline (DOD)
↓
Patron / Matron
↓
Gate Keeper / Security
↓
Boarding Students
2.1 Head Teacher / Principal / School Admin
The Head Teacher / Principal has overall school authority.
The Boarding Management System does not need to duplicate all operational functions at this level.
The Head Teacher / Principal should primarily have:
•	Boarding overview
•	Reports
•	Monitoring
•	Escalation visibility
•	Historical records
•	Leave and attendance reports
•	Exception reports
________________________________________
3. Director of Discipline (DOD)
The DOD is the primary operational authority for the Boarding Module.
The DOD should have control over:
•	Dormitories
•	Boarding schedules
•	Boarding attendance windows
•	Dining schedules
•	Dining timings
•	Leave approval
•	Leave rejection
•	Parent-requested leave
•	Student-requested leave
•	Gate authorization
•	Boarding attendance monitoring
•	Missing attendance escalation
•	Boarding student status
•	Patron / Matron assignment
•	Boarding reports
•	Boarding exceptions
•	Operational notifications
The DOD must have a complete dashboard showing the current boarding situation.
________________________________________
4. Patron / Matron
There may be multiple Patrons and/or Matrons in the school.
A Patron/Matron must not automatically see all boarding students.
Their access must be controlled through Dormitory Assignment.
4.1 Assignment Logic
When creating or editing a Patron/Matron:
User → Boarding Role → Patron/Matron → Assigned Dormitories
The system should display a list of available dormitories.
The DOD/Admin can assign:
•	One dormitory
•	Multiple dormitories
A Patron/Matron should only see:
•	Assigned dormitories
•	Students belonging to assigned dormitories
•	Attendance of assigned students
•	Dining attendance of assigned students
•	Leave requests of assigned students
•	Boarding alerts related to assigned students
They should not have access to unrelated dormitories.
________________________________________
5. Boarding Student Profile
Every student assigned to the Boarding Module must have a complete boarding profile.
The following information should be available:
•	Student ID
•	Admission/Registration Number
•	Student Name
•	Class
•	Section
•	Gender
•	Parent/Guardian information
•	Parent mobile number
•	Boarding status
•	Dormitory
•	Room
•	Bed
•	Patron/Matron
•	Biometric ID
•	Student photograph
•	Current leave status
•	Current boarding status
________________________________________
6. Mandatory Student Photograph
A passport-size student photograph must be mandatory for every boarding student.
A student should not be considered fully boarding-ready until a valid photograph is uploaded.
Purpose
The photograph is a critical security layer.
The Gate Keeper must be able to visually compare:
Student → System Profile Photo → Physical Student
This prevents:
•	Identity substitution
•	Another student leaving using someone else's roll number
•	Unauthorized student exit
•	Manual identity manipulation
The Gate Keeper must have access to the student's profile photograph before allowing exit.
________________________________________
7. Boarding Status
The system should maintain a real-time boarding status for every student.
Recommended statuses:
•	IN_SCHOOL
•	IN_DORMITORY
•	ON_SHORT_LEAVE
•	ON_LONG_LEAVE
•	ON_MEDICAL_LEAVE
•	ABSENT
•	RETURNED
•	EXIT_PENDING
•	EXIT_APPROVED
•	OUTSIDE_SCHOOL
The exact UI terminology may be simplified, but the backend must maintain clear state values.
________________________________________
8. Leave Management
The Boarding Module must support two primary leave-request sources:
Option A – Student Initiated
Student verbally requests leave from the relevant Patron/Matron.
Option B – Parent Initiated
Parent requests leave through:
•	Parent Mobile Application
•	Phone call to DOD
•	Direct visit/request at school
Regardless of the request source, DOD remains the final operational authority for approval.
________________________________________
9. Student-Initiated Leave Workflow
Step 1 – Student Requests Leave
Student approaches the relevant:
•	Patron, or
•	Matron
The request may initially be verbal.
Step 2 – Patron/Matron Creates Request
The Patron/Matron logs into the portal and creates the leave request.
Required information:
•	Student
•	Leave type
•	Start date
•	Start time
•	Expected return date
•	Expected return time
•	Reason
•	Destination, if required
•	Parent/contact information
•	Supporting document, where applicable
Step 3 – Request Sent to DOD
The request appears in the DOD portal.
Step 4 – School Administration Visibility
The request may also be visible to authorized School Administration users for monitoring/reporting.
Step 5 – DOD Decision
DOD can:
•	Approve
•	Reject with comments 
•	Return for clarification
Step 6 – Parent Notification
The parent receives an application notification. (Upon approval or rejection.)
For applicable long/medical leave, the parent additionally receives an SMS.
________________________________________
10. Parent-Initiated Leave
Parents can request leave through:
Method 1 – Parent Application
Parent submits leave request through the mobile application.
Method 2 – Phone Call
Parent contacts the DOD.
Method 3 – Direct School Visit
Parent physically comes to school and requests leave.
In all three cases, the DOD remains the responsible authority.
________________________________________
11. Parent Phone/Direct Request Workflow
If a parent calls or physically visits the school:
1.	DOD verifies the parent/request.
2.	DOD creates the student's leave request in the system.
3.	DOD reviews the request.
4.	DOD approves the request.
5.	System generates the appropriate notifications.
6.	Relevant Patron/Matron receives approval.
7.	Gate Keeper receives exit authorization.
8.	Student becomes eligible for physical exit.
If the DOD creates and approves the request himself, the system should still maintain the complete audit trail.
Example:
Created By: DOD
Approved By: DOD
Approval Date/Time: System timestamp
Exit Authorized: Yes
________________________________________
12. Recommended Leave Types
The system should support configurable leave types rather than hard-coding only one or two types.
12.1 Short Leave
Recommended default categories:
1.	Few-Hours / Outing Leave
2.	Half-Day Leave
3.	Same-Day Leave
4.	Emergency Short Leave
The school may enable/disable these categories.
________________________________________
12.2 Long Leave
Recommended default categories:
1.	Weekend Leave
2.	Multi-Day Leave
3.	Home Leave / Vacation Leave
4.	Special Long Leave
________________________________________
12.3 Medical Leave
Medical leave should be a separate leave category because it requires stronger notification and escalation.
Recommended fields:
•	Medical leave reason
•	Start date (By Default current Date)
•	End date (Optional Field)
•	Medical notes
•	Medical document/attachment, if required
•	Parent/guardian information
________________________________________
13. Leave Approval Matrix
Leave Type	Request Source	Approval	Parent App	SMS
Short Leave	Student/Parent	DOD	Yes	Optional/Policy Based
Long Leave	Student/Parent	DOD	Yes	Yes
Medical Leave	Student/Parent	DOD	Yes	Yes
Emergency Leave	Student/Parent	DOD	Yes	Policy Based
The notification rules must be configurable by the ECA.
________________________________________
14. Medical Leave Notification
Whenever DOD approves a medical leave, the system must immediately send:
1.	Parent Mobile App notification
2.	Parent SMS
The purpose is to ensure that the parent is immediately aware of the student's medical-related leave and can contact the school if necessary.
________________________________________
15. Leave Approval Does Not Equal Physical Exit
This is a critical system design principle.
The system must distinguish between:
Leave Approved
and
Student Physically Exited School
Example:
Leave Approved → Student Still Inside School
Only after the Gate Keeper confirms the actual exit should the student become:
OUTSIDE_SCHOOL / ON_LEAVE
This prevents inaccurate records.
________________________________________
16. Gate Exit Process
Once DOD approves a leave:
The approval must become visible to:
•	Relevant Patron/Matron
•	Gate Keeper
The Gate Keeper should have a dedicated Approved Boarding Exits screen.
The screen should display:
•	Student photograph
•	Student name
•	Student ID
•	Class
•	Dormitory
•	Room
•	Leave type
•	Approved start time
•	Expected return time
•	Approval status
•	DOD approval information
________________________________________
17. Gate Keeper Verification
Before allowing the student to leave, the Gate Keeper must:
1.	Open approved leave record.
2.	View student photograph.
3.	Verify physical student against photograph.
4.	Verify student identity.
5.	Confirm that the leave is approved.
6.	Confirm exit.
The Gate Keeper must not manually create or approve leave.
________________________________________
18. Gate Exit Button
The action button should clearly represent the physical event.
Recommended button text:
“CONFIRM GATE EXIT”
Alternative:
“MARK AS EXITED”
The preferred option is:
CONFIRM GATE EXIT
When clicked:
•	System records exact exit timestamp.
•	Gate Keeper identity is recorded.
•	Student status changes to OUTSIDE_SCHOOL / ON_LEAVE.
•	Leave start timestamp is generated.
•	Student becomes visible as “On Leave” across the school system.
________________________________________
19. Exit Audit Record
The system must record:
•	Student
•	Leave ID
•	Gate
•	Gate Keeper
•	Exit date
•	Exit time
•	Device/session information where applicable
•	Approved leave reference
•	Actual exit timestamp
This record must never be silently overwritten.
________________________________________
20. System-Wide “On Leave” Status
Once physical exit is confirmed, the student's status must automatically change across the entire School Management System.
The student should appear as:
ON LEAVE
in:
•	School administration
•	Class-related views
•	Boarding
•	Parent App
•	Attendance-related screens
•	Student profile
•	Reports
•	Other relevant modules
The system should use a single source of truth for the student's current leave status.
________________________________________
21. Student Return
No manual leave closure should normally be required.
When the student returns to school:
1.	Student uses biometric attendance at the designated gate.
2.	Biometric system identifies the student.
3.	Shows on Patron/Matron’s Portal for return approval.
4.	System confirms return. (after the confirmation from Patron/matron )
5.	Current leave is automatically closed.
6.	Return timestamp is recorded.
7.	Student status changes from:
ON_LEAVE
to:
IN_SCHOOL
or appropriate boarding status.
________________________________________
22. Automatic Leave Closure
On successful return:
Leave Start: Actual Gate Exit Timestamp
Leave End: Actual Biometric Return Timestamp
The system should calculate:
Actual Leave Duration = Return Timestamp – Exit Timestamp
The originally approved duration should remain separately stored for comparison.
This allows reporting of:
•	Approved duration
•	Actual duration
•	Late return
•	Early return
________________________________________
23. Late Return
If the student returns after the approved return time, the system should flag:
LATE RETURN
The system should record:
•	Expected return
•	Actual return
•	Delay duration
The DOD should receive an alert/report.
parent notification for late return.
