28. Boarding Biometric Attendance
Biometric attendance is a core boarding security feature.
The responsibility for monitoring boarding biometric attendance belongs to the relevant Patron/Matron.
The system must show:
•	Total students
•	Attendance completed
•	Attendance pending
•	Students absent from biometric attendance
•	Students on approved leave
•	Students who have not returned from leave
•	Last attendance timestamp
________________________________________
29. Boarding Attendance Window
DOD must configure the attendance window.
Required settings:
•	Attendance Start Time
•	Attendance End Time
•	Grace Period
•	Applicable Dormitories
•	Applicable Classes/Groups, if required
Example:
Attendance Start: 8:00 PM
Attendance End: 9:00 PM
Final Counting: 9:30 PM
Only biometric events within the configured attendance window should count for that boarding attendance session.
________________________________________
30. Last Valid Attendance Rule
If a student scans multiple times during the attendance window, the system should maintain all raw biometric transactions.
However, the system should use the last valid biometric attendance within the configured window as the final attendance event for that session.
Raw biometric logs must remain available for audit purposes.
________________________________________
31. Attendance Window Completion
At the end of the configured attendance window:
The system automatically identifies:
Students who:
•	Attended
•	Did not attend
•	Are on approved leave
•	Have returned from leave
•	Have invalid/missing biometric data
Students who are on approved leave must not be treated as missing boarding attendance.
________________________________________
32. Missing Boarding Attendance
If the attendance window closes and a student:
•	Has no valid attendance
•	Is not on approved leave
then the system should immediately notify:
1.	Relevant Patron/Matron
2.	DOD
The student should be placed in:
ATTENDANCE MISSING
status.
________________________________________
33. Parent Escalation – One Hour Rule
Parents should not immediately receive an SMS/Notification when the attendance window first closes.
Instead:
Stage 1
Attendance window closes.
Notification:
•	Patron/Matron
•	DOD
Stage 2
System starts a 1-hour escalation timer. (Must configurable from DoD Portal)
Stage 3
If attendance is still not recorded within the next hour and the student is not on leave:
Parent receives:
•	Mobile App notification
•	SMS (if Active from ECA)
This avoids unnecessary parent alerts caused by temporary delays.
________________________________________
34. Attendance Escalation Timeline
Example:
9:00 PM
Attendance window closes.
9:00 PM
Patron/Matron + DOD notified.
9:00–10:00 PM
Grace/escalation period.
10:00 PM
If attendance is still missing:
Parent App Notification + SMS.
If the student is subsequently identified, the system records the actual biometric event and preserves the escalation history.
________________________________________
