72. Critical Business Rules
The following rules must be treated as mandatory development requirements:
1.	DOD is the final operational authority for boarding leave.
2.	Patron/Matron is the first operational communication point for student-requested leave.
3.	Multiple Patrons/Matrons must be supported.
4.	Patron/Matron access must be dormitory-based.
5.	A Patron/Matron must only see assigned dormitory students.
6.	Student photograph is mandatory for boarding students.
7.	Gate Keeper must verify photograph before exit.
8.	Gate Keeper cannot approve leave.
9.	Physical exit must be separately confirmed.
10.	Exit confirmation must create an immutable timestamped event.
11.	Approved leave alone must not mark a student as physically outside.
12.	Student must become “On Leave” only after physical exit confirmation.
13.	Return must normally be automatic through biometric attendance.
14.	Manual leave closure should not be part of the normal workflow.
15.	DOD controls boarding attendance timing.
16.	DOD controls dining timing.
17.	Boarding attendance must operate within a configured time window.
18.	Last valid biometric event within the window is the final attendance event.
19.	Students on approved leave must be excluded from missing attendance.
20.	Missing attendance initially alerts Patron/Matron and DOD.
21.	Parent SMS must be delayed until the configured escalation period, currently one hour.
22.	Medical leave approval must immediately trigger Parent App + SMS.
23.	Long leave approval must trigger Parent App + SMS.
24.	All critical actions must be audited.
25.	Biometric raw transactions must be preserved.
26.	Existing biometric APIs/devices should be reused.
27.	Boarding status must synchronize with the wider School Management System.
28.	Dining attendance must respect current student leave status.
29.	Parent must only see their own children.
30.	Gate Keeper must only see information required for security/exit operations.
