74. Recommended Final Architecture
The Boarding Module should be designed around the following principle:
DOD = Operational Control
Patron/Matron = Dormitory Operations
Gate Keeper = Physical Security & Exit Verification
Biometric System = Physical Presence Verification
Dining Department = Meal/Menu Management
Parent App = Parent Communication & Request Channel
School Administration = Oversight & Reporting
This separation of responsibilities is critical.
The system should not allow one role to perform the complete workflow alone unless that role is specifically authorized by the DOD's permission model.
________________________________________
75. Core Design Principle
The Boarding Module should always distinguish between:
What the system says should happen
and
What physically happened.
For example:
Leave Approved does not mean the student has left.
Attendance Expected does not mean the student is present.
Return Expected does not mean the student has returned.
The system must confirm physical events through:
•	Gate confirmation for exit
•	Biometric transaction for return
•	Biometric transaction for boarding attendance
•	Authorized manual exception only where necessary
This principle will make the Boarding Module much more reliable from both an operational and security perspective.
