77. Conclusion
The redesigned Boarding Management Module should function as a centralized operational control system rather than simply a student attendance and leave feature.
The Director of Discipline (DOD) remains the central authority for boarding operations. Patrons and Matrons manage their assigned dormitories, while the Gate Keeper controls the physical exit process. Biometric devices provide objective physical-presence data, and the Parent Mobile Application/SMS system provides communication with parents.
The most important architectural principle is the separation of:
Request → Approval → Physical Exit → Leave Status → Physical Return → Automatic Closure
Similarly, boarding attendance must follow:
Attendance Window → Biometric Presence → Missing Student Detection → Internal Escalation → Parent Escalation
This structure provides the school with:
•	Better student security
•	Clear accountability
•	Accurate boarding records
•	Real-time student status
•	Controlled leave management
•	Reliable attendance
•	Better parent communication
•	Full operational auditability
•	Reduced manual intervention
•	Clear role separation
•	Scalable support for multiple dormitories and boarding staff
The existing generic Boarding module should therefore be redesigned around these workflows and business rules rather than simply adding individual features on top of the current implementation.

Scope & Compatibility Statement
This document applies exclusively to the Boarding Management Module and its related workflows. The requirements and features defined in this document must not modify, replace, remove, or negatively affect any existing roles, users, dashboards, permissions, workflows, APIs, modules, or system functionality outside the Boarding Module. All existing users and roles must continue performing their current responsibilities as they do today. Where an existing user or role is identified as being operationally related to Boarding, the Boarding-specific functions defined in this document shall be treated as additional responsibilities/features for the Boarding Module only, and must not be considered a replacement for their existing system functionality.

